cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MultiView Product Renderer in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CADshot"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Danyal
    family-names: Sarfraz
version: 1.13.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Danyals-code/Addon-for-MultiView-Rendering-AMVR"
abstract: >-
  A Blender add-on that turns CAD (STEP, IGES) and mesh files into three kinds of
  standardized image set: multiple clay views of a product's form, patches of the
  materials in a texture pool, and products rendered across every combination of
  view and texture. Canonical camera rigs or published protocols, studio lighting,
  clay, line-art, depth, normal and part-ID passes, camera poses, COCO and BOP
  annotations, vector engineering drawings, seeded randomization, and a provenance
  manifest with Croissant metadata. Formerly MultiView Product Renderer.
keywords:
  - Blender
  - CAD
  - STEP
  - multi-view rendering
  - material patches
  - CMF
  - synthetic data
  - dataset generation
  - engineering drawings
